
This is a simple example of how to use the OrgC/C++ library in the C mode.
It runs in two stages:

Program test1.c reads Employee records (name,salary), and puts them into two
parallel linked lists. It sorts the two lists, prints them, and saves the data
to disk (file "myFile").

Program test2.c reads the data from disk, and prints it again.

How to run the test:
       test1 inp out1     ... prints the first result to file out1
       test2 > out2       ... prints the second result to file out2
       comp out1 out2     ... the two files should be the same
